    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Production Process</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Our Manufacturing Process</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Our baby clothing manufacturing follows a structured process designed to ensure consistent safety, fabric quality, and construction durability. The process typically spans 60-75 days for first-time orders including sampling and production, with 45-60 days for repeat orders using approved fabrics and patterns. Baby clothing requires particular attention to safety testing and secure construction to meet international children's product standards.</p>
        
        <p>The process begins with specification review, where we analyze your requirements including fabric preferences (organic cotton, bamboo, cotton blends), product category, age group, size chart, and safety requirements. Our team provides feedback on technical feasibility and may suggest modifications to optimize manufacturability while maintaining safety standards. This stage takes 2-3 days and ensures technical alignment before sampling begins. For baby clothing, we pay particular attention to fabric safety certification and construction safety considerations.</p>
        
        <p>Fabric sourcing and development follows specification review, taking 10-15 days for standard fabrics and 15-20 days for custom fabric development. Baby clothing fabrics undergo rigorous testing for chemical safety, softness, and durability before approval. We test fabrics for shrinkage, color fastness, and pilling resistance to ensure quality through repeated washing. All fabrics must meet OEKO-TEX Standard 100 requirements for baby skin safety. If you require custom fabric development for specific colors or prints, we coordinate with mills to produce sample yardage for testing and approval.</p>
        
        <p>Sample development for baby clothing takes 15-20 days for basic items and 20-25 days for complex garments like outerwear. Initial samples focus on construction and basic fit, with subsequent samples refining fit details, fabric softness, and safety features. We provide detailed measurement reports comparing samples to your specifications and conduct wash testing to verify dimensional stability. Baby clothing samples require particular attention to seam safety, closure security, and overall comfort. You may request multiple sample rounds to perfect the design.</p>
        
        <p>Safety testing is a critical step in baby clothing sampling that we conduct on all samples. We evaluate closure security to ensure snaps, zippers, and buttons cannot detach during use, test for loose threads or components that could pose choking hazards, verify that decorative elements are securely attached, and assess fabric softness for baby skin comfort. For sleepwear, we conduct flame resistance testing as required by US and EU regulations. This safety-focused testing ensures that the final product meets international children's product safety standards and provides parents with assurance of safety.</p>
        
        <p>Pattern grading for baby clothing requires careful attention to proportional scaling across different age groups. The relationship between various measurements must be maintained through grading to ensure consistent fit across sizes. Our pattern makers use graded measurement systems that account for these relationships, producing size sets from newborn to size 12 that maintain proportional fit appropriate for each age group. Grading takes 3-5 days for basic items and 5-7 days for complex garments with multiple components. Grading includes verification of age-appropriate fit proportions.</p>
        
        <p>Bulk production for baby clothing spans 30-40 days from fabric receipt for basic items like onesies and rompers. Sleepwear and outerwear typically require 35-45 days. Cutting is performed with attention to grain direction for woven items to ensure consistent drape. Sewing lines are staffed by operators trained in baby garment construction, with particular expertise in secure seam techniques, safe closure attachment, and delicate fabric handling. Quality checkpoints at each sewing operation verify seam integrity, closure security, and construction accuracy with safety focus.</p>
        
        <p>Final quality inspection uses AQL 2.5 standards for major defects and AQL 4.0 for minor defects, with additional testing for baby clothing-specific criteria. Inspection includes measurement verification against graded size charts, wash testing on random samples to verify dimensional stability, and construction quality verification with particular attention to safety features. We also conduct pull testing on closures and visual inspection for any loose components. Detailed inspection reports with photos are provided before shipment, and any safety-related defects result in immediate rectification before goods leave our facility.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Materials</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Fabric & Material Options</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Fabric selection is critical to baby clothing performance, affecting safety, comfort, durability, and care requirements. We offer multiple fabric options optimized for different climates, seasons, and safety requirements. All fabrics are certified safe for baby skin through OEKO-TEX Standard 100 certification.</p>
        
        <p>Organic cotton certified by GOTS (Global Organic Textile Standard) provides the safest option for baby clothing, grown without synthetic pesticides or fertilizers and processed without harmful chemicals. Organic cotton typically ranges from 120-160 GSM for baby garments. The fabric offers natural softness, breathability, and familiar comfort that parents trust. Organic cotton costs approximately 15-20% more than conventional cotton but provides assurance of chemical safety and environmental sustainability. GOTS certification requires traceability throughout the supply chain, providing additional credibility for organic claims.</p>
        
        <p>Combed cotton undergoes an additional combing process that removes shorter fibers and impurities, resulting in smoother, stronger yarn with enhanced softness. Combed cotton typically ranges from 130-170 GSM and offers superior softness and reduced pilling compared to carded cotton. The combing process produces fabric that is particularly suitable for baby clothing due to its smooth texture and durability. Combed cotton is ideal for everyday baby wear where softness and durability are both priorities. The additional processing adds approximately 10-15% to fabric cost but delivers noticeable quality improvement.</p>
        
        <p>Bamboo fabric offers sustainable softness with natural antimicrobial properties that help reduce odor and bacterial growth. Bamboo viscose is produced from bamboo grass, a rapidly renewable resource, and features a luxurious hand feel similar to silk. Bamboo fabrics typically range from 120-150 GSM and are naturally moisture-wicking and temperature-regulating. The fabric has excellent drape and remains soft through repeated washing. Bamboo is more sustainable than conventional cotton, requiring less water and no pesticides. Bamboo fabrics cost approximately 10-15% more than conventional cotton but appeal to eco-conscious parents seeking sustainable options.</p>
        
        <p>Cotton blends combine cotton with polyester or other fibers to enhance durability and easy care while maintaining comfort. Typical blends range from 80/20 to 50/50 cotton-polyester ratios, with higher cotton content providing more natural feel. These blends typically range from 140-180 GSM and offer balanced performance at competitive prices. The polyester component reduces shrinkage compared to 100% cotton, improving dimensional stability and reducing wrinkling. Cotton blends are ideal for everyday baby wear where easy care is prioritized alongside comfort and durability.</p>
        
        <p>Fleece provides warmth and comfort for cold weather baby clothing. Fleece is typically a synthetic fabric with a brushed surface that traps heat against the body. Fleece baby clothing ranges from 180-220 GSM, providing substantial warmth for cold climates. The fabric is lightweight for its warmth, making it suitable for outerwear without adding bulk. Fleece is quick-drying and maintains its insulating properties even when damp. Fleece is ideal for winter outerwear, blankets, and cold-weather sleepwear. The synthetic nature of fleece requires careful selection to ensure OEKO-TEX certification for chemical safety.</p>
        
        <p>Modal is a semi-synthetic fiber produced from beech wood pulp, offering exceptional softness with excellent drape. Modal typically ranges from 120-150 GSM and resists pilling better than cotton. The fabric has a smooth, silky hand feel that remains soft through repeated washing. Modal is breathable and moisture-wicking, making it comfortable for baby wear. The beech wood used for modal is harvested from sustainably managed forests, making modal an eco-friendly option. Modal is ideal for premium baby clothing positioning where luxurious softness is a priority.</p>
        
        <p>All fabrics used in baby clothing production must pass OEKO-TEX Standard 100 certification, which tests for harmful substances including heavy metals, pesticides, formaldehyde, and other chemicals. This certification is essential for baby clothing due to the sensitivity of infant skin and the tendency of babies to mouth clothing items. We provide OEKO-TEX certificates for each fabric lot, enabling you to substantiate safety claims in your marketing materials and meet retailer requirements for children's product safety certification.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-wrapper">
        <table class="comparison">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Fabric</th>
              <th>GSM Range</th>
              <th>Key Properties</th>
              <th>Best For</th>
              <th>Price Tier</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Organic Cotton</td>
              <td>120-160</td>
              <td>Safe, chemical-free, soft</td>
              <td>Infant wear, safety-focused</td>
              <td>$$$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Combed Cotton</td>
              <td>130-170</td>
              <td>Soft, smooth, durable</td>
              <td>Everyday wear, comfort</td>
              <td>$$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Bamboo</td>
              <td>120-150</td>
              <td>Sustainable, antimicrobial, soft</td>
              <td>Eco-conscious, premium</td>
              <td>$$$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Cotton Blends</td>
              <td>140-180</td>
              <td>Durable, easy care, practical</td>
              <td>Everyday, active children</td>
